{"title":"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e361a761d74597fa29719dd014ca09b504e8993f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_k\\}_{k=1}^{2011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> be the sequence of real numbers defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/b/a0b6ceb87b15ac3c911f9c510607228963083a11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=0.201,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb4209d568b46fbe97940913d12cfb637b8627f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=(0.2011)^{a_1},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/f/78fdcf4019c3cd1be24e85cf375113f93c314521.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=(0.20101)^{a_2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/290dc3e820f2bd82a85bbb85201bdc7474a818c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4=(0.201011)^{a_3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" />, and in general, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/6/006ecf77f807aa89b66a8e2e9f281e579e7cd062.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_k=\\begin{cases}(0.\\underbrace{20101\\cdots 0101}_{k+2\\text{ digits}})^{a_{k-1}}\\qquad\\text{if }k\\text{ is odd,}\\\\(0.\\underbrace{20101\\cdots 01011}_{k+2\\text{ digits}})^{a_{k-1}}\\qquad\\text{if }k\\text{ is even.}\\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"353\" height=\"85\" />\n</p><p>Rearranging the numbers in the sequence  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e361a761d74597fa29719dd014ca09b504e8993f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_k\\}_{k=1}^{2011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> in decreasing order produces a new sequence  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/6/8d66d40a30444f8ae9a83825e11bf2b209521f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{b_k\\}_{k=1}^{2011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"19\" />.  What is the sum of all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71d3552ede761f8ad3403c1f57d77eeeb3e036dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le k \\le 2011$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/896f64b93a5121b3d5662f170924bbc366409bb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k=b_k?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/feb2bce2dfe6d7808eb889cbf248f36c1cc9418e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 671\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1006\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 1341\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2011\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"475\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we must understand two important bull functions: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/b/72b1bc89fda62367b5751b5da84a84427b829b21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = b^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9cabde1685a6e1d28759e7155a6ac61afd3e7409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; b &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />(decreasing exponential function), and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/4213e726791694044572bfd03e8afbc160fc793a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) = x^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/a/6da5c768d3e309c1b5337c06bf5ad8df078c5c01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />(increasing power function for positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />). <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is used to establish inequalities when we change the <i>exponent</i> and keep the <i>base</i> constant. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is used to establish inequalities when we change the <i>base</i> and keep the <i>exponent</i> constant.\n</p><p>We will now examine the first few terms.\n</p><p>Comparing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eed842f7b67a87d316f9d6dc88db311ac0e9a037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a_1 = (0.201)^1 &lt; (0.201)^{a_1} &lt; (0.2011)^{a_1} = a_2 &lt; 1 \\Rightarrow 0 &lt; a_1 &lt; a_2 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"562\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/0/d109f4a2a0b6160d1b9afe90e0acafc5267f19ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a_1 &lt; a_2 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Comparing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/6/b565fe90952c29c5009d379d2604a7e95b3f448e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a_3 = (0.20101)^{a_2} &lt; (0.20101)^{a_1} &lt; (0.2011)^{a_1} = a_2 &lt; 1 \\Rightarrow 0 &lt; a_3 &lt; a_2 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"605\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Comparing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8573da61f9c2a0a5625697b825f084b4f85f4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a_1 = (0.201)^1 &lt; (0.201)^{a_2} &lt; (0.20101)^{a_2} = a_3 &lt; 1 \\Rightarrow 0 &lt; a_1 &lt; a_3 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"571\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e9fdc64275a5f823fde49b269fe9febc089bb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a_1 &lt; a_3 &lt; a_2 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"165\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Comparing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e28850813a5321d2a8ae3c0510457a7337975ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/4913dfe66b117bcceb6268263931df7496256b64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a_3 = (0.20101)^{a_2} &lt; (0.20101)^{a_3} &lt; (0.201011)^{a_3} = a_4 &lt; 1 \\Rightarrow 0 &lt; a_3 &lt; a_4 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"624\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Comparing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e28850813a5321d2a8ae3c0510457a7337975ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4aed73017fa1e0bd3828219199326cef32862af5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a_4 = (0.201011)^{a_3} &lt; (0.201011)^{a_1} &lt; (0.2011)^{a_1} = a_2 &lt; 1 \\Rightarrow 0 &lt; a_4 &lt; a_2 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"624\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/240a683079e53be7e74d39903b5ad4377711564e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a_1 &lt; a_3 &lt; a_4 &lt; a_2 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"206\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Continuing in this manner, it is easy to see a pattern(see Note 1).\n</p><p>Therefore, the only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/6045dddd3ce9b6ca0c5b71d5818e66b6db41f66a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" /> is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883807b888d0d32072e4eb449c6e19a60e429aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(k-1006) = 2011 - k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />. Solving gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/4/9944d3f96345f7107f4542272c849cd355f05935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} 1341}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"76\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Note 1</b>:\nWe claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408e16253719f6a4c4c7e05c55ee386b567492da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a_1 &lt; a_3 &lt; ... &lt; a_{2011} &lt; a_{2010} &lt; ... &lt; a_4 &lt; a_2 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"407\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>We can use induction to prove this statement. (not necessary for AMC):\n</p><p>Base Case: We have already shown the base case above, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/0/d109f4a2a0b6160d1b9afe90e0acafc5267f19ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a_1 &lt; a_2 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Inductive Step: \n</p><p>Rearranging in decreasing order gives \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26bbe751aa3751ab38263d20f0781943e70ebed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &gt; b_1 = a_2 &gt; b_2 = a_4 &gt; ... &gt; b_{1005} = a_{2010} &gt; b_{1006} = a_{2011} &gt; ... &gt; b_{2010} = a_3 &gt; b_{2011} =  a_1 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"724\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Start by looking at the first few terms and comparing them to each other. We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfe569c0beabb06044562a1c0c763c52f646e6d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &lt; a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/143a851be8cbfd4af1b85ec6c58cd16b7bf5f760.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &lt; a_3 &lt; a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"12\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af382ebb735e2145f858de892018f67e03a816b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3 &lt; a_4 &lt; a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"12\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d3624f9b4d602794693649bb55788f3dc9c64947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3 &lt; a_5 &lt; a_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"12\" /> ... \n</p><p>From this, we find the pattern that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bdaa81850a56e45eeaa3ac2f1346b61a87e21c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k-1} &lt; a_{k+1} &lt; a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Examining this relationship, we see that every new number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> will be between the previous two terms, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/6352edc6b969aefe0cbeb900b23a65ae60db8cd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a366b8b3e317783a60eeca856e2efbe1f5ff7755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is the smallest number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is the largest number, and that all odd terms are less than even terms. Furthermore, we can see that for every odd k, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d1e93b15ba08a5e607141e5331123db6bb6076.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k &lt; a_{k+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />, and for every even k, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/4/284f17bacef4b4a5ea621eab7e9a48a1f9745bd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k &gt; a_{k+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>This means that rearranging the terms in descending order will first have all the even terms from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de1c6840452dda74ad04d513c6a6a8928d69fa0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />, in that order, and then all odd terms from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b045f36b2962ec608554541c4c8a2573fb9dd009.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, in that order (so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/0/300aa8dd411175cba15b945e43dc2498f2f9023f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{b_k\\}_{k=1}^{2011} = {a_2, a_4, a_6, ... a_{2008}, a_{2010}, a_{2011}, a_{2009}, ... a_5, a_3, a_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"436\" height=\"19\" />).\n</p><p>We can clearly see that there will be no solution k where k is even, as the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th term in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e361a761d74597fa29719dd014ca09b504e8993f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_k\\}_{k=1}^{2011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> will appear in the same position in its sequence as the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea7ee8a282949fd853a01537ec7a2b55e56f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />th term does in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e361a761d74597fa29719dd014ca09b504e8993f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_k\\}_{k=1}^{2011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" />, where k is even. Therefore, we only have to look at the odd terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, which occur in the latter part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bdec4394870e8a713538ce428bea9d41c8775f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Looking at the back of both sequences, we see that term k in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e361a761d74597fa29719dd014ca09b504e8993f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_k\\}_{k=1}^{2011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> progresses backwards in the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f4e2de7a3a88832b95879443649595fb95c803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012 - k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" />, and that term k in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e361a761d74597fa29719dd014ca09b504e8993f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_k\\}_{k=1}^{2011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> progresses backwards in the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/7/d9725e28ef5cf646a27665952959be316b1b4826.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />. Setting these two expressions equal to each other, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2b5b001d120ed78f226ed5d50b1b1c06b490cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$671$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>However, remember that we started counting from the back of both sequences. So, plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2b5b001d120ed78f226ed5d50b1b1c06b490cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$671$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> back into either side of the equation from earlier, we get our answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/4/9944d3f96345f7107f4542272c849cd355f05935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} 1341}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"76\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>Sorry for the sloppy explanation. It's been two years since I've tried to give a solution to a problem, and this is the first time I've really used \\LaTeX. But I think this solution takes a different approach than the one above.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2012amc12a/255\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2012amc12a/255</a>\n</p><p>~dolphin7\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A\">2012 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.p